    description: "Source: an outside reader (a fresh LLM session given only the help output and the cached files) reviewed a hypergumbo 9.2.0 self-run on 2026-11-13, cache f36c63310c791188/results/49869475df136c86/eb6b68753d44e259. Every claim below was re-checked against those files and the code on dev d6a8a140e7.\n\nA tiered view slims nodes to nine fields (compact_node) and leaves the rest of the map at full size. Measured on the self-run:\n- limits is 10.3 KB in every tier. skipped_passes holds 69 records, 67 of them the same reason (\"no files matched\"), one per analyzer. failed_files holds 12 records in which 7 share one reason sentence.\n- Edges keep 13 or 14 fields (id, edge_key, origin, origin_run_id, confidence_source, rank_score, meta, derived_from, ...), 595-1,131 bytes each as written. src, dst, type, line and confidence are about 300.\n- Each node id is a long string that appears five to eight times across nodes, edges, entrypoints and features: 22-25% of the 16k and 64k files.\n- features is 23% of the 16k file. Every feature carries a query block; five of the ten hold a single node. The slices themselves are already written to survey.slices/.\n- profile (2.4 KB), reproducibility_context (1.5 KB) and supply_chain_summary (1.3 KB) are copied whole.\n\nASK. Define what a tiered view carries for each section, as compact_node does for nodes: a tier projection for edges, a grouped form for records that differ only in one key (N analyzers, one reason), and a decision on whether features and ids are repeated or referenced. The decision has to keep every disclosure a reader needs (which passes were skipped and why, which files failed) while removing the repetition.\n\nThis item is about economy. The sibling invariant (a tier file exceeds its stated budget) is about the contract; it can be satisfied without this, by giving nodes less.\n\nGENERALITY (owner, 2026-11-13). The fix must be a rule that holds for any repository and any language. The hypergumbo self-run is only where the defect was seen. A fix keyed to this repo's paths or file names, or one that works only for Python, does not close this item.\nThe repetition scales with the number of registered analyzers and with repo size, so the saving has to be stated as a rule on record shape, never as a list of this repo's keys. Acceptance: bytes per tier before and after on at least three repositories that are not hypergumbo, with node and edge counts per tier."  # 2948
    fields: {}  # 2948
